ook><name>YAMAMOTO CHEMICALS, INC.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJITA SHIGEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUMAGAE YOJIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TERAO HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJITA, SHIGEO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUMAGAE, YOJIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TERAO, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Novel phthalocyanine compounds which have absorption in a near-infrared region of from 700 to 1,000 nm and reduced absorption in the visible region and hence are suitable for use in a near-infrared absorption filter for plasma displays, a secret ink, etc. The compounds are represented by general formula (I). The near infrared absorbent is characterized by comprising any of the compounds. (In the formula, R1 to R8 each represents alkyl or alkoxyalkyl; X1 to X8 each represents sulfur or &gt;NR9, provided that X1, one of X3 and X4, one of X5 and X6, and one of X7 and X8 each is sulfur and that X2, the other of X3 and X4, the other of X5 and X6, and the other of X7 and X8 each is &gt;NR9; R9 represents optionally substituted acyl or optionally substituted aroyl; and M represents two hydrogen atoms, a divalent metal, or a derivative of a trivalent or tetravalent metal).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des composés de phthalocyanine dotés d'une absorption du proche infrarouge allant de 700 à 1,000 nm et une absorption réduite dans la zone visible, ce qui permet de les utiliser dans un filtre d'absorption du proche infrarouge pour affichages au plasma, encre sympathique, etc. Les composés sont représentés par la formule générale (I). L'absorbant du proche infrarouge est caractérisé en ce qu'il renferme n'importe lequel des composés. (Dans la formule, R1 à R8 représentent chacun alkyle ou alcoxyalkyle; X1 à X8 représentent chacun le soufre ou &gt;NR9, pour autant que X1, un de X3 et X4, un de X5 et X6 et un de X7 et X8 soient chacun du soufre et que X2, les autres de X3 et X4, de X5 et X6 et de X7 et X8 soient chacun &gt;NR9; R9 représente facultativement acyle substitué ou aroyle substitué; et M représente deux atomes d'hydrogène, un métal bivalent ou un dérivé d'un métal trivalent ou tétravalent).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>